{
  "id": "Compound::DB00331 - Gene::4714",
  "verbalization": "Metformin is shown to interact with Ndufb8 through a shared pathway involving Nadh Dehydrogenase (ubiquinone) Activity. The evidence suggests that Metformin binds to Ndufa12 and Ndufv3, both of which participate in the same enzymatic activity, leading to Ndufb8 being a participant in this process. This indicates that Metformin may influence Ndufb8 through a common mechanism involving the Nadh Dehydrogenase complex. The high scores in all three paths suggest a strong, consistent relationship between Metformin and Ndufb8, likely mediated by the shared role of Ndufa12 and Ndufv3 in the activity of Ndufb8. The mechanism appears to involve the inhibition of a critical enzymatic process, which could be a key target for Metformin's therapeutic effects. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Metformin exerts its effects on Ndufb8 through a mechanism involving the Nadh Dehydrogenase complex, potentially by modulating its activity.",
